A minimal compatibility shim that translates Linux runuser(1) invocations
into FreeBSD su(1) calls.

Linux runuser syntax:  runuser USER -s SHELL -c COMMAND
FreeBSD translation:   su -m USER -c COMMAND

The -s SHELL argument is intentionally ignored; FreeBSD su -m uses the
target user's login shell or /bin/sh, which is sufficient for all known
callers (e.g., FreePBX pm2 module).

This allows Linux software that hardcodes runuser(1) to work unmodified
on FreeBSD without patching individual source files.
